   "item": {
    "subject_key": "biology",
    "unit_number": 3,
    "topic_code": "3.3",
    "topic_title": "Cellular Energy",
    "stem": "A cell builds a polymer from monomers in a reaction that requires energy input. A second reaction releases more energy than polymer synthesis requires. The cell couples these reactions. Which statement explains how this coupling supports polymer synthesis?",
    "choices": [
     {
      "choice_key": "A",
      "choice_text": "Coupling creates new energy that the cell uses to build the polymer.",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "Energy-creation misconception: Coupling transfers energy between processes; it does not create energy. Cells obey conservation of energy even when they build ordered structures. Fix: Identify the source of energy before explaining how a cellular process uses it."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "B",
      "choice_text": "The reactions only need to occur simultaneously; no energy transfer between them is necessary.",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "Coincidence-as-coupling error: Simultaneous reactions are not necessarily coupled. Polymer synthesis requires a connection that allows energy from the releasing reaction to drive the energy-requiring process. Fix: Check whether released energy actually supports the process, rather than merely being released nearby."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "C",
      "choice_text": "Coupling allows the cell to recycle energy indefinitely, eliminating its need for additional energy input.",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "Energy-recycling misconception: Energy transfers include losses of usable energy, so coupling cannot power cellular work indefinitely. Living systems require continuing energy input to maintain organization and function. Fix: Trace energy input and energy loss instead of assuming energy cycles like matter."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "D",
      "choice_text": "Energy released by the second reaction supplies the energy required for polymer synthesis.",
      "is_correct": true,
      "rationale": "Polymer synthesis requires an energy input. Coupling connects an energy-releasing reaction to this energy-requiring process, allowing released energy to drive synthesis rather than being unavailable for that work."
     }
    ]
   },
